# ccproxy — local dev env. Copy to .env, edit, then:
#
#   go run ./cmd/ccproxy serve     # from inside sources/
#
# Note the PACKAGE path (./cmd/ccproxy), not the file (./cmd/ccproxy/main.go) —
# `go run` on a single file skips sibling files in the same package
# (token.go etc.) and you'll get "undefined: runToken".
#
# .env is auto-loaded from CWD by godotenv; existing env vars always win.
# The production template lives in ../deploy/env.example.
#
# Behavior (verbosity, effort, model aliases, workspaces, passthrough,
# claude binary path) lives in config.yaml — see config.yaml.example.
# Env here is only for secrets and deploy-time wiring.

# OPTIONAL. First-boot bearer seed in ccp_<prefix>_<secret> format.
# Leave empty to let ccproxy auto-mint a token on first boot — it is
# printed once in the startup banner; copy it immediately.
# CCPROXY_TOKEN=

# Listener address. Loopback only by default for local dev.
CCPROXY_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:4141

# Optional. When set, ccproxy serves Prometheus /metrics on this address
# WITHOUT auth — only bind to localhost or a private network.
# CCPROXY_METRICS_LISTEN=127.0.0.1:9101

# Where ccproxy puts its SQLite token DB and ephemeral workspaces.
# Default would be /var/lib/ccproxy (root-owned); use a local path for dev.
CCPROXY_STATE=./var-state

# Optional explicit path to config.yaml. If unset, ccproxy looks at
# $CCPROXY_STATE/config.yaml then ./ccproxy.yaml. Overridden by --config.
# CCPROXY_CONFIG=config.yaml
